      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Business::GoCardless versions before 1.01 for Perl accept forged webhooks when a configured webhook secret is undef or empty.\n\nsignature_valid uses each configured secret as the HMAC key, and nothing rejects undef or an empty string, both of which Digest::SHA treats as an empty key. A secret read from an unset environment variable, or an empty entry in a list of rotated secrets, is used as is.\n\nA remote attacker can sign a forged webhook with an empty key and have it accepted as sent by GoCardless.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
